  "finalMessage": "ROUND 4a INDEPENDENT REVIEW (Read-only)\n\nStatus: PASS with findings (no Hard Blockers, 1 Should-fix, 2 Nits).\n\nStatic checks:\n- S110-S114 passed (.agents/checks/check_r4a.py: S110 four ordered statuses, S111 removed events/tags gone, S112 stored isProphylaxis preserved, S113 MedicationStatusBadge defined once, S114 old codex wording removed).\n- Unit tests: not run (Gradle daemon socket binding blocked in sandbox).\n\nFindings:\n1. [Should-fix] MedicationEditor.kt:282 / PatientEditor.kt:511:\n   `listOf(\"\").plus(choices).forEachIndexed` in `ChoiceGroup` prepends `\"\"` (\"Unknown\"), so `medStatusChoice` displays 5 choices (\"Unknown\", \"Active\", \"Completed\", \"Discontinued\", \"Patient non-compliant\") rather than \"exactly the four statuses\" specified by Q204 and D22. Selecting \"Unknown\" sets draft status to `\"\"`.\n2. [Nit] PatientPrintHtmlGenerator.kt:201:\n   `val displayedMeds = patient.medications.take(MAX_PRINT_MEDICATIONS)`\n   Does not filter using `isOngoingMedication`; Completed and Discontinued medications are included under the \"Active Medications\" printed report section (with their respective status badges).\n3. [Nit] MedicationEditor.kt:282:\n   `ChoiceGroup` uses standard M3 `FilterChip` styling rather than theme container colours matching `MedicationStatusBadge` as referenced in Q204 (\"Colours come from Q205\").\n\nVerification checklist:\n- Active + old non-compliant flag: handled correctly in workspace count (`isOngoingMedication`), card badge (`MedicationStatusBadge`), summary, print, and draft loading (`effectiveMedicationStatus`).\n- Data loss: `isProphylaxis` and `isNonCompliant` preserved in DB schemas, Room entities, Dao, commands, backup/restore, and DraftMapping.\n- Editor: preset selection no longer touches prophylaxis; previous medication reset resets to \"Active\" and clears adverse/notes/dates; More section auto-expands when end date, notes, or adverse effects are present; testTags and 48dp touch targets preserved.\n- Badges & tokens: `MedicationStatusBadge` uses M3 container/onContainer token pairs with >= 4.5:1 contrast in light and dark themes.\n- Wording: \"Codex\" and \"Prophylaxis\" removed from visible UI, print badges, and summary prefixes.\n- Cleanliness: deleted strings (`is_prophylaxis`, `prophylaxis_badge`, `therapeutic_badge`, `patient_non_compliant`, `non_compliant_badge`) verified unused across main, test, androidTest, and res. No touched files outside ALLOW list.",
